      "content": "Definition: Understandability refers to how easily developers can comprehend and maintain the test code.\n\nTask: Improve the understandability of the test `TestPaxChronology_test_isLeapYear_loop.java` (path:- /Users/tenghaha/Projects/New_Agent_understandability_improvement/data/original/threeten-extra/manual/testcases/TestPaxChronology/TestPaxChronology_test_isLeapYear_loop.java). The refactored code must be syntactically correct and compilable against the provided CUT signatures. Do not alter the runtime behaviour of the original test: the same methods must be called with the same arguments and produce the same expected outcomes.\n"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I'll write the improved version. The original has several understandability issues:\n1. Dozens of unused `data_*` methods that bloat the file and obscure intent\n2. An anonymous `IntPredicate` lambda that encodes the leap year rule without explanation\n3. No comments explaining what the Pax leap year rule actually isThe improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version extracts the leap year logic into a named `isPaxLeapYear` helper method with a Javadoc comment explaining the Pax rule, removes the ~100 lines of unused data provider methods that cluttered the original file, and adds failure messages to the `assertEquals` calls to make test failures immediately diagnostic."
    }
